# Bundled ONNX models are byte-exact artifacts: assets/models/manifest.json
# records a sha256 for each one, and the VSIX build refuses to package a file
# that does not match. Git must therefore never rewrite them.
#
# `-text` is what does that. Without it, a Windows checkout with the default
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF in the JSON files — config.json goes
# from 650 to 675 bytes and its hash changes — and `npm run package:dev` fails
# with "Staged model checksum mismatch". The .onnx files are binary and were
# never affected, which is why only the JSON ones broke.
#
# These patterns are anchored to this file's directory because they contain a
# slash, so they must name the real location. The models live in the core
# package (they ship inside the npm package); the earlier `assets/models/**`
# rules matched a repository-root directory that no longer holds them, leaving
# every model file with no attributes at all.
#
# No filter=lfs here, deliberately: the files are committed as ordinary blobs
# and `git lfs ls-files` is empty, so declaring an LFS filter would convert them
# to pointers on the next write and hand a broken checkout to anyone without
# git-lfs installed. Moving them into LFS is a separate decision.
packages/core/assets/models/** -text
packages/core/assets/models/manifest.json -text

# Keep the historical root-level location covered too, in case models are ever
# staged there again.
assets/models/** -text
